# ⚠️ Unvalidated comment-derived sha in the diff command — fixed (hardening)

`getDiffBetweenCommits` now format-checks **both** heads before they may reach the command string:

```javascript
// js/common/gitOps.js
var DIFF_SHA_RE = /^[0-9a-fA-F]{7,40}$/;

function isDiffSha(value) {
    return DIFF_SHA_RE.test(String(value));
}

function getDiffBetweenCommits(fromSha, toSha, workingDir) {
    ...
    if (!isDiffSha(fromSha) || !isDiffSha(toSha)) {
        console.warn('Diff-of-diff skipped — non-sha head value in verdict record:', ...);
        return '';
    }
```

Exactly the suggested defense-in-depth line: a git short/full sha is 7–40 hex chars; anything else — a branch name, an injection payload, truncated garbage from an edited verdict comment — never reaches `cli_execute_command`. The degradation contract is unchanged (skip → `''` → full-diff review, same as a failed diff command), so this stays pure hardening with no behavior change for legitimate rounds.

## Tests (TDD — written first, failing before the fix)

`js/unit-tests/test_gitOps.js`, suite `gitOps.getDiffBetweenCommits — the diff-of-diff`:

- a command-injection-shaped `fromSha` / `toSha` → `''`, **zero commands run**, warn logged;
- a branch name (`origin/main`) is rejected — the diff-of-diff is sha-only by contract;
- boundary acceptance: 7-char short form, 17-char mid form, 40-char full form, uppercase hex;
- 6-char / 41-char values rejected (boundary lengths).

All pass; the pre-existing force-push/failure-path tests stay green.

Fixed in `<commit>`.

# ⚠️ Second identical `getPrComments` fetch — fixed (one shared round-trip)

Steps 6.5 and 6.6 now share a single fetch, exactly as suggested:

```javascript
// js/preparePRForReview.js, action() steps 6.5 + 6.6
var prComments = prCommentsForContextSteps(ctx.scm, prOutcome.pr.number);
writeFindingRegistryContext(ctx, prOutcome.pr.number, prComments);
writeNewHunksContext(ctx, prDetails, prComments);
```

Details:

- `prCommentsForContextSteps` wraps the read in the non-fatal contract: a transport failure logs a warn and yields `null`, and both steps skip quietly — the same observable behavior as a provider without `getPrComments`. The fetch therefore never leaks a failure into `action()`'s fatal catch (the "comment-read failure is non-fatal" characterization test pins this).
- Both writers accept the shared list as an optional third parameter; omitted → the step fetches its own (the direct-call shape the unit tests exercise). `null` → skip quietly, contract preserved unchanged.
- The helper formerly named `prCommentListForRegistry` is renamed `normalizedPrComments` — it is no longer registry-specific (this also resolves the digest note at `js/preparePRForReview.js:282`).

## Tests (TDD — written first, failing before the fix)

- `steps 6.5+6.6 read the PR comment list ONCE per review round` — a counting `getPrComments` mock asserted to be called exactly 1× (failed with 2 before the fix);
- `one shared fetch still feeds BOTH injections when a moved head injects pr_new_hunks.txt` — 1 fetch AND the `pr_new_hunks.txt` write still happen;
- `a shared-fetch transport failure is non-fatal and skips both steps quietly` — no `pr_findings.md`/`pr_new_hunks.txt` writes, review start succeeds;
- direct-call tests for the optional-comments contract on both writers.

This also dropped `writeNewHunksContext`'s complexity (the duplicate fetch was one of its guard clauses), helping the 🚨 ratchet finding at the same time.

Fixed in `<commit>`.

# 💡 `sameHead` hand-copy — fixed (one shared matcher)

The prefix-equality rule now lives once, in `reviewVerdicts.js` (the module that owns verdict-for-head matching), and both consumers delegate:

```javascript
// js/common/reviewVerdicts.js — exported next to latestVerdictForHead
function sameHead(a, b) {
    if (!a || !b) return false;
    var x = String(a);
    var y = String(b);
    if (x === y) return true;
    if (x.length >= 7 && y.indexOf(x) === 0) return true;
    if (y.length >= 7 && x.indexOf(y) === 0) return true;
    return false;
}
```

